cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: "delphir: Structured Delphi and RAND/UCLA Analysis for Consensus Studies"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Ming
    email: yangpluszhu@sina.com
repository-code: https://github.com/yangpluszhu/delphir
url: https://github.com/yangpluszhu/delphir
abstract: >-
  Protocol-first R toolkit for Delphi studies, RAND/UCLA appropriateness
  panels, and COMET core outcome set surveys. Locks consensus rules before
  analysis, summarises ordinal ratings with medians and agreement rates,
  classifies items, assesses between-round stability, prepares controlled
  feedback, and writes ACCORD, DCAT and CREDES aligned reports.
keywords:
  - Delphi
  - consensus
  - RAND/UCLA
  - COMET
  - ACCORD
  - DCAT
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
